WEBVTT

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.240
Right.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.040
Well, here it is.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.040
(gateway rattling)

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.640
(grunting)

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.560
(grunts)

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:42.560
(indistinct chatter)

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.600
Huh.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.800
(Theseus) German Ministry of Magic?

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.000
Yes.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.000
(fireworks whistling and bursting)

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.640
I take it we're here for a reason.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.080
Yes, we have a tea
ceremony to attend,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.320
and if we don't hurry
up, we'll be late.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.280
Jacob, stay with the group.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.400
(fireworks continue bursting)

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.600
(crowd chanting in distance)

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.640
(crowd) Santos! Santos! Santos!

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.840
Santos! Santos! Santos!

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:27.280
(yells)

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.800
(crowd continues chanting)

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.760
Evening...

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.240
Helmut.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.880
-Theseus. -(guard speaks German)

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.000
(Theseus) Hey, hey.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.640
They're with me.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.880
(Lally sighs)

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.880
(fireworks continue bursting)

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.760
(crowd continues chanting)

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.320
Santos! Santos! Santos!

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.160
(chanting continues)

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.040
Incendio.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.080
(crowd cheering)

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.280
(crowd clamoring)

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.840
(lightning crackling)

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.880
I take it we're not here
for the finger sandwiches.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.640
Uh, no, I have a message to
deliver.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.960
A message?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.160
To who?

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.440
(man) Mr. Vogel, it's a
pleasure to be here.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.880
It's an honor to meet you.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.520
You are joking.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:51.680
No.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.160
(Jacob) What am I even doing here?
Let's go outside.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.920
I'm not very good in
these situations.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.120
These situations?

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.000
With all the people,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.360
-the fancy people. -(clicks tongue)

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:03.760
Hello.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.360
(in German accent) I
saw you enter the room

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.080
and I thought to myself,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.280
Edith, that's an
interesting-looking man.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.280
Jacob Kowalski.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.440
How are you? Very nice to meet you.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.280
And where is it you hail from, Mr.
Kowalski?

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.480
(smacks lips) Queens.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:21.880
Ah!

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.720
(Newt) Sorry, Herr Vogel. Sorry,
I wonder if I could have a word?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.000
Oh!

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.920
Merlin's beard, it's Mr.
Scamander, isn't it?

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.680
Herr Vogel...

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.000
(whispers indistinctly)

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.360
I have a message from a
friend, and it cannot wait.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.000
Do what is right...

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.280
not what is easy.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.760
He said it was important
that I reach you tonight,

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.000
that you hear them
tonight, the words.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.880
It's time, sir.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.600
(Vogel whispering) Is he here?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.400
In Berlin?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.120
(in normal tone) No, of course not.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.480
Why leave Hogwarts when the
world outside is burning?

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.320
I thank you, Mr. Scamander.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.600
(cup clinking)

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.360
(clinking stops)

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.720
(crowd applauding)

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.520
Thank you.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.880
Thank you.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.840
I see many familiar
faces here tonight.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:09.520
Colleagues, friends...

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:11.800
foes.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.960
(crowd laughs)

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.080
Within the next 48 hours,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.640
you, along with the rest
of the Wizarding World,

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.040
will choose our next great leader.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:26.840
A choice that will shape our
lives for generations to come.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.000
I have little doubt that, no
matter who should triumph,

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.480
the Confederation will
be in able hands.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.120
Liu Tao.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:38.960
(crowd applauds)

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.520
Vicencia Santos.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.200
(softly) Thank you, thank you.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.680
It's in moments such as
these we are reminded

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:58.800
that it is this peaceful
transfer of power

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.800
which marks our humanity

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.760
and demonstrates to the world
that, despite our differences,

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.920
all voices deserve to be heard...

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.720
even voices which many
may find disagreeable.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.040
(suspenseful music playing)

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.480
Newt.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.680
Any of those lot look
familiar to you?

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.680
(Vogel continues
speaking indistinctly)

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.200
Paris. The night that Leta...

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:28.360
(Theseus whispers) They
were with Grindelwald.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.360
(suspenseful music continues)

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.520
Mm.

